From 8bc6098ebf007aaf04c9a4c552916694d0bd34cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Deng, Bing" <bing.deng@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 16:28:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Port Point-LIO to ROS2 and add benchmarking instrumentation

1. Port the codebase from ROS1/catkin to ROS2/ament_cmake, swapping
   roscpp for rclcpp, livox_ros_driver for livox_ros_driver2, and
   the fast_lio Pose6D message for a local struct instead.
2. Add ROS2 YAML configs for Avia, Mid-360, and a UrbanLoco Velodyne
   HDL-32E dataset, plus a launch file that takes the config path
   as an argument.
3. Add an opt-in profiling pipeline (ENABLE_PROFILING) that times
   each pipeline stage and streams per-frame latency to a CSV
   through a lock-free ring buffer and dedicated writer thread, so
   the hot path pays no logging cost when profiling is off.
4. Anchor the interval timers to a monotonic clock instead of
   CLOCK_REALTIME so an NTP step mid-run can't corrupt a
   measurement, while keeping the transport timestamp on
   CLOCK_REALTIME so it still lines up with PTP-stamped headers.
5. Expose MP_PROC_NUM_CPUSET so the OpenMP thread count can be
   pinned at configure time, and align the Avia config's
   point_filter_num and blind range with the FAST-LIO2 side of the
   benchmark pair for a fair comparison.
6. Fix a segfault on point clouds with no time field by checking
   the PointCloud2 field list before reading PCL's otherwise
   uninitialized time value.
7. Fix the UrbanLoco config's IMU period, revert init_map_size to
   the upstream default of 10, and create the Log directory before
   opening the profiling CSV so a fresh checkout doesn't fail
   silently on first run.

Signed-off-by: Deng, Bing <bing.deng@intel.com>
